CONTEXT BoxGuardedEdit IN ENGLISH
-- CRUD rights are fixed per interface object, so rights that differ per atom sit in a box whose term selects the atoms.
-- Here a choice whose home is the application can be edited and deleted, and a choice that lives elsewhere cannot.

REPRESENT Text TYPE ALPHANUMERIC
REPRESENT Artefact TYPE OBJECT
CLASSIFY Choice ISA Artefact
RELATION text[Choice*Text] [UNI]
RELATION homeHere[Artefact*Artefact] [PROP]

POPULATION Choice CONTAINS [ "here", "elsewhere" ]
POPULATION homeHere[Artefact*Artefact] CONTAINS [ ("here", "here") ]
POPULATION text[Choice*Text] CONTAINS [ ("here", "old here"), ("elsewhere", "old elsewhere") ]

INTERFACE Choice : I[Choice] cRud BOX <FORM>
    -- The term ends on I[Choice] outside the intersection, because a field of Choice needs a box with that target:
    -- the compiler drops I[Choice] from I[Choice];homeHere;I[Choice] and gives that box the target Artefact.
    [ "Edit" : (I[Choice] /\ homeHere);I[Choice] cRuD BOX <FORM>
        [ "Text" : text cRUd ]
    , "Contents" : I cRud BOX <FORM>
        [ "Text" : text cRud ]
    ]

ENDCONTEXT
